{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB04920 - MONDO_grouped_1200_1134_15512_5080_100078",
  "verbalization": "Clevidipine is associated with Hypertension through a series of indirect pathways, as evidenced by its indication for Hypertensive Disorder, which in turn is linked to other drugs that treat Hypertension. This suggests that Clevidipine may exert a role in the pathophysiology of hypertension through mechanisms that are not directly specified in its indication. The presence of multiple drugs (Mibefradil, Hydralazine, and Methyldopa) that are indicated for Hypertension further supports the idea that Clevidipine may be part of a broader network of drugs influencing blood pressure regulation. The shared relationship between Clevidipine and Hypertension implies a potential mechanism involving vascular or renal effects, though the exact nature of this mechanism remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of drug-repurposing and the need for further investigation into Clevidipine's role in hypertension.",
